Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||03-08-2001||11:56 AM||||Lisa, as long as it wasn't registered with Namezero or something like that (in which case you're possibly out of luck..) then it's easy to get a cheap host for it.. you just need to set up an account, and then change the domain records. If you did register it with namezero, then you'll likely be stuck paying their high fees to change it. I try to stay away from services like that.. there's ALWAYS a catch.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.123cheaphosting.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.123cheaphosting.com/</A>  is $10 <A HREF="http://www.canaca.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.canaca.com</A>  is $10 <A HREF="http://www.cheapest-hosting.com/bare.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cheapest-hosting.com/bare.html</A>  is $5<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 03-08-2001).]||||reg||3
