Z||000014||LarryB||03-08-2001||03:45 PM||||Lisa, your domain is registered through register.com.  2 advantages of using them are that 1) you (well, Faith does, I assume she's your mom) maintains control over the domain and 2) you can use the register.com nameservers if you want to point to your machines.  (Registration info is public record and is easily obtainable.)<P>Since your stuff is now on a Geocities server you'd have to do a fair amount of editing and some changes but it is doable.  Expect to have to find or create some of the background stuff you are using now or substitute something else instead occasionally. You should even be able to point your existing geocities url to the new url using some redirect code. <P>BTW a good reference book is O'Reilly's HTML/XHTML: The Definitive Guide if you want to really get into hardcoding web pages instead of using a FrontPage-type toolkit. ||||reg||1
